The meshes in this folder are NASA's Ingenuity Mars Helicopter 3D model (science.nasa.gov/resource/
mars-ingenuity-helicopter-3d-model, mars.nasa.gov resource 25043, file 25043_Ingenuity_v3.glb, sha256
d9ebff90d0475d0be0f9dc241e69bb1700d86c702a1f289578c35f4fefc9f19f; also mirrored in github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources).
Credit: NASA/JPL-Caltech, used under the NASA media usage guidelines (nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media:
NASA's 3D model files "generally are not subject to copyright in the United States"); NASA is acknowledged here and
does not endorse PteroSim.

Changes made here: the model is cut by node into body.glb (bus, solar panel, mast parts, the four legs, the cameras)
in the glb's own frame, and rotor_upper.glb / rotor_lower.glb (nodes rotors_01 / rotors_02) each about its own hub,
with every node transform baked into the vertices and each file carrying only the materials, samplers and textures its
meshes use. The NASA insignia and the JPL logotype, which are not in the public domain, were painted out of the "blade"
colour atlas and the solar panel's roughness and normal maps; the US flag decal was kept. Nothing else -- geometry,
UVs, the other textures -- was changed.
